  "justification": "CLASSIFICATION: STATISTICALLY_INTERESTING_BUT_NOT_ECONOMIC. Predictive models (AR(3), Linear Multi) exhibit statistically significant out-of-sample explanatory power for BTCUSDT funding rates (R2_OOS ~70%, RMSE reduced from 1.15 to 0.60 bps, DM p-value < 0.001). However, directional sign accuracy (90.8% - 92.5%) provides less than +1.2% incremental accuracy over the naive majority-class baseline (91.31%). Furthermore, the roundtrip transaction cost to unwind and re-establish a delta-neutral carry position (19.0 bps Maker, 36.0 bps Taker) is 17x to 68x greater than the average avoided negative funding loss (-0.28 bps; max -1.12 bps). Consequently, all dynamic carry switching policies result in catastrophic net underperformance (-300.13 to -2,054.84 USDT) relative to passive continuous carry. The signal has no standalone or incremental economic viability."
